{"commit_sha":"259ef83a3428df890cd08585ce4a41ce1bb27f7f","category":"pattern","title":"Move blocking Cloudflare API calls off the UI thread using mpsc channels","body":"Direct synchronous CF API calls were blocking the TUI, so all network operations (sync, route management, token verification) were moved to background threads communicating via mpsc channels. The TUI now renders instantly from local cached data while CF syncs asynchronously, with input blocked during loading to prevent duplicate triggers. This establishes a BgResult enum pattern for routing async results back into app state.","files":["src/app.rs","src/cloudflare.rs","src/main.rs"],"tags":"async concurrency tui mpsc background-threads architecture"},
{"commit_sha":"259ef83a3428df890cd08585ce4a41ce1bb27f7f","category":"decision","title":"Lock domain suffix when renaming service subdomains","body":"The new `m` rename keybinding on the Services tab only allows editing the subdomain prefix, keeping the domain suffix locked. This prevents accidental cross-domain renames and keeps the UX scoped to the common use case of just changing the service name.","files":["src/app.rs","src/ui.rs"],"tags":"ux services rename decision"},
{"commit_sha":"259ef83a3428df890cd08585ce4a41ce1bb27f7f","category":"bugfix","title":"Service URLs hardcoded https:// regardless of tunnel protocol","body":"Non-HTTP tunnel services (ssh, tcp, rdp) were displayed with a hardcoded https:// prefix, which was misleading since those protocols aren't web-based. The fix makes the Services tab protocol-aware, deriving the correct URL scheme from the tunnel's actual protocol configuration.","files":["src/ui.rs","src/cloudflare.rs"],"tags":"bugfix protocol ui services"}
]
